From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Walsh <contact.me@thejustinwalsh.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 13:24:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: a persistent VRAM page window for the host-mapped
 attention K/V (LLAMA_KV_PAGE_WINDOW)

With LLAMA_KV_HOST_MAPPED (0012/0021) the sparse (QSA) attention's K/V live
in pinned host memory, and 0014 converts the ~2,051 cells each query
selects to f16 from there on EVERY step of every QSA layer: all of them
cross PCIe each time, though consecutive steps' selections are expected to
overlap (Strata's premise; not measured here). This is Strata's VRAM page window (Niko1221/Strata,
src/kernels/cuda/kv_stream.cu @ d551edf, MIT; --kv-resident), done in the
conversion step, not in the attention kernel:

- per K or V cache tensor in a host-mapped buffer: a page table (block ->
  slot or -1), 4-cell pages (Strata qsa.hpp:115), a pool of n_slots pages
  in VRAM holding the cache's own quantized rows (q8_0 or q4_0, so a hit is
  the same bytes as the host row), and Strata's residency map (slot_block,
  slot_stamp, slot_ref, miss lists);
- before 0014's conversion, one resolve kernel (Strata resolve_kernel:
  hits stamp the call's epoch and their CLOCK reference bit, a miss is
  claimed once, a CLOCK sweep takes one victim per miss and never a slot
  the call uses) and one copy kernel (Strata copy_kernel, 96 x 128) bring
  the pages the index lists name, and page 0, into the pool; the conversion
  kernel then reads each cell from its slot, or from the host when its page
  is not resident (a call naming more pages than the window holds);
- writers drop pages instead of writing through (Strata owns its writers,
  llama.cpp's are ggml ops and host copies): a SET_ROWS node into a windowed
  tensor invalidates the pages of the rows it names, any other op writing
  into one resets it, and a host write through the buffer (set / memset /
  copy / clear: a state restore, the prompt cache) resets every window of
  the buffer. All capturable; the maps are allocated when the tensor is, so
  a graph captured before the first attention call still invalidates;
- Off by default. LLAMA_KV_PAGE_WINDOW=<cells> per K or V tensor (1 =
  Strata's shipped 32,768, setup.py:1022); never below Strata's floor of
  20,480 (layer.cpp:522: one call's pages, and the verify window's) unless
  LLAMA_KV_PAGE_WINDOW_FLOOR says so (tests). A call whose lists could name
  more pages than the window holds (n_lists x (n_kv_max / 4 + 2) + 1) does
  not use it. The pool is allocated by the first call, outside a graph
  capture. GGML_CUDA_KV_PAGE_STATS=1 logs the hit rate every 1,024 graphs.

Tests: tests/test-kv-page-window-model.cpp (CPU: the resolve kernel's
algorithm run phase by phase over 12,000 fuzzed calls, windows of 3 to
5,000 slots; the kernel is changed for fewer than 1,024 slots, where
Strata's sweep gives two threads one slot) and tests/test-kv-page-window.cpp
(CUDA, one device: a llama-shaped host-mapped cache, q8_0 and q4_0, window
on vs off bit for bit over cold, hot, evicting and 4-query steps, the host
copy of resident pages poisoned, a write into resident pages, the same with
invalidation switched off (it must fail), a host write, the window's size,
a window too small for a call).

Not run on a GPU when written: the CPU model passes; test-kv-page-window
compiles and has not been run, nor has the window been measured.
